IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ky-ktap`

-- KTAP -- the seat of the applicant (the parent or relative with whom a needy child lives, applying for or receiving
-- KTAP).
--
-- "How much KTAP would we get each month? What is the most a family our size can get? Are our savings under the limit? I
-- turned down a job: am I barred? My pay went up: by when must I report it?" Every answer is built from ky-ktap.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `KTAP -- my questions`

§§ `How much we would get`

@export How much KTAP cash assistance would our benefit group get each month (KRS 205.200(2); 921 KAR 2:016 Sections 3 to 5, 9)?
GIVEN `the number of eligible persons in our benefit group` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your KTAP benefit group: the dependent children, their parent or parents in the home, and eligible siblings
      `the cabinet's cost-of-living factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The factor by which the cabinet has raised the 921 KAR 2:016 figures for Social Security cost-of-living adjustments since 2023 (1 if you want the printed figures)
      `our liquid assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The benefit group's countable liquid assets: cash, bank accounts and the like, not counting excluded resources
      `our gross monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The benefit group's total gross monthly earnings (including a parent in the home)
      `how many of us work` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the benefit group are employed full-time or part-time
      `our dependent care disregard` IS A NUMBER @desc Child care paid to a caregiver outside the benefit group, allowed up to $175 a month per person for full-time work, $150 for part-time, $200 for a child under two (0 if none)
      `we are in the six months of the 50 percent disregard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this month is one of the six months in which the first 50% of earnings is disregarded
      `we lost the earnings deductions this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, without good cause, a worker reduced, quit or refused work in the last 30 days, or did not report a pay increase within 10 days
      `our gross monthly unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The benefit group's other monthly income: unemployment, social security (not SSI), child support received, and so on
      `child support deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support received and kept before you were told you are eligible, or assigned and forwarded to the cabinet (0 if none)
      `our excluded unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Unearned income that 921 KAR 2:016 Section 5(2) excludes (0 if none)
GIVETH A `KTAP result`
`How much KTAP would we get` MEANS
    `the KTAP determination` `the number of eligible persons in our benefit group` `the cabinet's cost-of-living factor` `our liquid assets`
        (`Monthly income` WITH
            `gross earned income` IS `our gross monthly earnings`
            `employed members of the benefit group` IS `how many of us work`
            `dependent care disregard` IS `our dependent care disregard`
            `in the six months of the fifty percent disregard` IS `we are in the six months of the 50 percent disregard`
            `earnings deductions lost under Section 5(4)` IS `we lost the earnings deductions this month`
            `gross unearned income` IS `our gross monthly unearned income`
            `child support deducted under Section 5(3)(c) or (d)` IS `child support deducted`
            `excluded income under Section 5(2)` IS `our excluded unearned income`)

@export What is the most KTAP pays a benefit group of our size each month, the payment maximum (921 KAR 2:016 Section 9(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the number of eligible persons in our benefit group` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your KTAP benefit group
      `the cabinet's cost-of-living factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The cabinet's cost-of-living factor since 2023 (1 for the printed figures)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is our payment maximum` MEANS `payment maximum` `the number of eligible persons in our benefit group` `the cabinet's cost-of-living factor`

@export What is the gross monthly income limit for a benefit group of our size (921 KAR 2:016 Section 9(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the number of eligible persons in our benefit group` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your KTAP benefit group
      `the cabinet's cost-of-living factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The cabinet's cost-of-living factor since 2023 (1 for the printed figures)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is our gross income limit` MEANS `gross income limit` `the number of eligible persons in our benefit group` `the cabinet's cost-of-living factor`

@export Are our liquid assets within the KTAP limit of $10,000 (921 KAR 2:016 Section 3(2))?
GIVEN `our liquid assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The benefit group's countable liquid assets
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are our assets within the limit` IF `is within the resource limitation` `our liquid assets`

§§ `Work and reporting`

-- Only after a refusal of work or training.
@export I refused to register for work, or to take suitable training or a suitable job: am I barred from public assistance (KRS 205.200(7))?
GIVEN `the cabinet found me potentially responsible and gave me notice and a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cabinet determined you to be potentially responsible and gave you notice and an opportunity for a hearing
      `I refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refused to register with the state employment service, to accept suitable training, or to accept suitable employment
      `I had good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had good cause for refusing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred for refusing work` IF
    `is barred by 205.200(7)` `the cabinet found me potentially responsible and gave me notice and a hearing` `I refused` `I had good cause`

-- Only for a recipient whose pay has gone up.
@export My earnings went up: by what date must I report it to keep my KTAP earnings deductions (921 KAR 2:016 Section 5(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the day my earnings changed` IS A DATE @desc The day the increase in earnings happened
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I report the increase` MEANS `the day my earnings changed` PLUS 10

-- Only after the cabinet finds EBT cash was misused.
@export For at most how many months can the cabinet stop my cash benefits for misusing EBT cash (KRS 205.193(3)(b))?
GIVEN `which violation this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for a first violation, 2 for a second, 3 or more for a third
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Most months stopped for EBT misuse` MEANS `the most months of disqualification under 205.193(3)` `which violation this is`
